claim.claim-text:
transmitting a first radar transmit signal (306) using an antenna array (212) of the radar system (102);
receiving a first radar receive signal (308) using the antenna array (212), the first radar receive signal (308) comprising a version of the first radar transmit signal (306) that is reflected by at least one object, the at least one object comprising at least one user (302);
generating complex radar data (246) based on the first radar receive signal (308);
analyzing the complex radar data (246) using a machine-learned model to detect a change in the radar system's frame of reference;
determining that the radar system (102) is moving based on the detected change in the radar system's frame of reference;
determining a relative motion of the at least one user (302) in accordance with the detected change in the radar system's frame of reference, the relative motion comprising motion of the at least one user (302) as observed from the radar system (102);
determining, by a gesture recognition module and based on the determined relative motion of the at least one user (302), that the at least one user (102) did perform a gesture; and
recognizing, by the gesture recognition module, the gesture of the at least one user (302).

transmitting a second radar transmit signal (306) using the antenna array (212) of the radar system (102);
receiving a second radar receive signal (308) using the antenna array (212), the second radar receive signal (308) comprising a version of the second radar transmit signal (306) that is reflected by at least one other object;
generating other complex radar data (246) based on the second radar receive signal (308); and
analyzing the other complex radar data (246) using the machine-learned model to determine that the radar system (102) is stationary.

determining relative motion of the first object based on the complex radar data (246);
determining relative motion of the second object based on the complex radar data (246); and
detecting the change in the radar system's frame of reference by using the machine-learned model to compare the relative motion of the at least one user (302) with the relative motion of the first object.

the at least one user (302) is stationary and the first object is stationary;
the at least one user (302) is stationary and the first object is moving; or
the at least one user (302) is moving and the first object is moving.

a complex range-Doppler map;
complex interferometry data;
multiple digital beat signals associated with the radar receive signal; or
frequency-domain representations of the multiple digital beat signals.

an antenna array (212);
a transceiver (214); and
a processor (216) and computer-readable storage media configured to perform any of the methods of claims 1 to 11.

a smartphone;
a smart watch;
a smart speaker;
a smart thermostat;
a security camera;
a vehicle; or
a household appliance.
